  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public Participation in Enforcement of Wildlife Laws in CAFTA-DR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve enforcement of wildlife trafficking laws in three CAFTADR countries (Dominican Republic, Guatemala, and Nicaragua), by strengthening the capacity of key community organizations through concrete wildlife conservation projects, increasing public awareness through a creative outreach campaign, and supporting coordination between civil society actors, national governmental authorities, and regional initiatives such as ROAVIS. .</narrative>
  </description>
